WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.458
Three years on

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:02.673
still no non-WebKit

00:00:02.484 --> 00:00:03.475
iPhone browser

00:00:04.014 --> 00:00:05.759
Mozilla says Firefox

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:06.502
daily use on

00:00:06.314 --> 00:00:07.032
iOS

00:00:07.104 --> 00:00:08.117
has doubled since

00:00:07.929 --> 00:00:09.367
Europe's Digital Markets

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.169
Act forced a

00:00:09.981 --> 00:00:11.301
browser choice screen

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:12.926
But nearly three

00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:13.870
years after Apple

00:00:13.681 --> 00:00:14.707
allowed other engines

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:15.202
in the EU

00:00:15.332 --> 00:00:16.216
and almost a

00:00:16.028 --> 00:00:17.160
year in Japan

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.280
nobody has shipped

00:00:18.092 --> 00:00:18.622
one

00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:20.144
To use Gecko

00:00:20.156 --> 00:00:21.087
Mozilla would have

00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:21.524
to ship a

00:00:21.335 --> 00:00:22.632
second Firefox app

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:23.646
and ask users

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:24.519
to move everything

00:00:24.331 --> 00:00:25.392
over by hand

00:00:25.531 --> 00:00:26.332
It calls it

00:00:26.144 --> 00:00:27.028
a trap door

00:00:27.558 --> 00:00:28.572
Full story on

00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:29.279
the dashboard
